{
  "describe": "AutoBayes M0 model\n  formula   : y ~ x + (1 | county) + (1 | year)\n  family    : gaussian, identity link\n  data      : n = 60 observations, J = 6 levels of county; J = 5 levels of year\n  levels county: 0=C0, 1=C1, 2=C2, 3=C3, 4=C4, 5=C5\n  levels year: 0=Y0, 1=Y1, 2=Y2, 3=Y3, 4=Y4\n\nLinear predictor\n  mu_i = a_c + (x_x - mean(x_x)) * b_x + u_county[county_i] + u_year[year_i]\n  Predictors are centred at their sample means (center_predictors=True, as in\n  brms and Bambi).\n  a_c is the expected response at the predictor means (group effect zero); the\n  prior on the intercept applies to a_c. The posterior reports the raw-scale\n  intercept a = a_c - sum_p mean(x_p) * b_p, computed after sampling.\n\nGroup effects (non-centred)\n  u_county[j] = sd_county * z_county[j], z_county[j] ~ Normal(0, 1), j = 0..5\n  u_year[j] = sd_year * z_year[j], z_year[j] ~ Normal(0, 1), j = 0..4\n  Independent priors across factors; group effects are not mean-centered.\n\nPriors\n  a_c ~ Normal(mu=0, sigma=1.5)\n  b_x ~ Normal(mu=0, sigma=1)\n  sd_county ~ HalfNormal(sigma=0.8)\n  sd_year ~ Exponential(lam=2)\n  sigma ~ HalfNormal(sigma=1)\n\nLikelihood\n  y_i ~ Normal(mu_i, sigma)\n\nPyMC variables sampled (value space)\n  sigma_log__              log(sigma)\n  Intercept                a_c\n  x                        b_x\n  1|county_sigma_log__     log(sd_county)\n  1|county_offset          z_county\n  1|year_sigma_log__       log(sd_year)\n  1|year_offset            z_year\nDeterministic: 1|county = u_county, 1|year = u_year, mu = linear predictor",
